## std/loom.pengu
## Algoritmos de listas: generación de secuencias, cortes, ventanas, plegados,
## combinaciones, conjuntos sobre listas ordenadas, búsqueda, edición
## estructural y estadística.
##
## Todo el módulo son **funciones de módulo** (`calling loom.chunks with xs, 2`);
## no se declara ningún `enchanting` para no invadir los métodos de `std.tally`.
## La API concreta de 0.14.x/0.15.0 (`list of int`) se conserva **firma por
## firma**; las adiciones Pengunic usan `Pair` (`std.oracle`) o un núcleo
## genérico (`shard T`).
##
## ## Ownership
## Ninguna función muta ni libera sus entradas: solo las lee y devuelve listas
## nuevas auto-banishables (o escalares), incluidas las internas de `chunks`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import std.loom
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var xs as list of int is calling loom.range with 1, 6, 1
##     var total as int is calling loom.sum with xs
##     calling spark.println with "total={total}"
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Notas de diseño
## - **Funciones de módulo, no métodos.** La superficie heredada es de funciones
##   (`calling loom.sum with xs`); los métodos de lista viven en `std.tally`.
## - **Tipos heredados intactos.** `enumerate`, `pairwise` y `zip_longest`
##   siguen devolviendo `list of list of int`; las variantes con `Pair` son
##   nombres **nuevos** (`enumerate_pairs`, `pairwise_pairs`, `min_max`).
## - **Núcleo genérico.** Los `generic_*` y `flatten_generic` son el núcleo
##   `shard T`; las concretas delegan en ellos con `of int`. Un cuerpo genérico
##   no puede invocar a otro: cada núcleo es autocontenido.
## - **Alias sin toolchain.** `@deprecated` no existe: el único alias (`flatten`)
##   reenvía y lo anuncia en su docstring.
## - **Tests internos.** El harness `_expect*` usa `spark.panic`; `std.ward`
##   arrastraría `std.scrolls`/`std.oracle` (en reescritura) a loom.
## - **Límites del codegen en `test`.** Dentro de un bloque `test` el compilador
##   no resuelve un `weave` de módulo usado como *valor* (emite el nombre sin
##   prefijo) ni los nombres que otro módulo del bundle también exporta (p. ej.
##   `std.tally.flatten`), así que los `test` llaman a núcleos privados `_*_int`
##   y `scan_left`, `zip_with_op`, `is_partitioned`, `windowed` y `flatten` se
##   cubren en `tests/std_programs/loom.pengu`.
##
## ## Migración
## | Antes (0.14.x/0.15.0) | Ahora (0.15.0) |
## |---|---|
## | `take` / `skip` / `chain` / `repeat` | iguales; núcleo genérico `calling loom.generic_take of T with xs, n` |
## | `calling loom.chunks with xs, n` | igual, o `calling loom.chunk_every with xs, n, n` |
## | `calling loom.windows with xs, n` | igual, o `calling loom.windowed with xs, n` |
## | `calling loom.pairwise with xs` | igual, o `calling loom.pairwise_pairs with xs` (`Pair`) |
## | `calling loom.enumerate with xs` | igual, o `calling loom.enumerate_pairs with xs` (`Pair`) |
## | `calling loom.zip_with with a, b, op` | igual, o `calling loom.zip_with_op with a, b, f` |
## | `calling loom.flatten` / `min_int` / `max_int` | iguales; nuevos `flat_map_identity` y `min_max` |
## | `calling loom.range with 5, stop, step` | igual; nuevo `calling loom.unfold_range with 5, count, step` |
## | (nuevo) | `calling loom.is_partitioned with xs, predicate` |

# --- Imports ------------------------------------------------------------

import std.arithmancy
import std.oracle
import std.spark

# --- Constantes públicas ------------------------------------------------

## Versión del módulo loom.
const LOOM_VERSION as string is "0.15.0"

# --- Generación de secuencias -------------------------------------------

## Secuencia `[start, end)` avanzando `step`; `step == 0` devuelve `[]`.
weave range with start as int, end as int, step as int is 1 into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var current as int is start
    if step > 0:
        while current < end:
            calling out.push with current
            set current is current + step
    else if step < 0:
        while current > end:
            calling out.push with current
            set current is current + step
    return out

## `value` repetido `times` veces; `times <= 0` devuelve `[]`.
weave repeat with value as int, times as int into list of int:
    return calling _repeat_shard of int with value, times

## Progresión aritmética de `count` elementos (`start, start + step, …`).
##
## Cuenta elementos en vez de comparar contra un tope: `count <= 0` da `[]`.
weave unfold_range with start as int, count as int, step as int is 1 into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var current as int is start
    var i as int is 0
    while i < count:
        calling out.push with current
        set current is current + step
        set i is i + 1
    return out

# --- Cortes y composición -----------------------------------------------

## Primeros `n` elementos de `items`; `n > len` recorta y `n < 0` da `[]`.
weave take with items as list of int, n as int into list of int:
    return calling generic_take of int with items, n

## Elementos de `items` a partir del índice `n`; `n < 0` equivale a `n == 0`.
weave skip with items as list of int, n as int into list of int:
    return calling _drop_shard of int with items, n

## Concatenación de `a` y `b` en una lista nueva.
weave chain with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    return calling generic_chain of int with a, b

# --- Bloques y ventanas -------------------------------------------------

## Bloques consecutivos de hasta `n` elementos; `n <= 0` devuelve `[]`.
weave chunks with items as list of int, n as int into list of list of int:
    return calling _chunk_every_int with items, n, n

## Bloques de hasta `n` elementos tomados cada `step` posiciones.
##
## `step == n` equivale a `chunks`; `step < n` solapa y `step > n` salta.
## `n <= 0` o `step <= 0` devuelven `[]`.
weave chunk_every with items as list of int, n as int, step as int is 1 into list of list of int:
    return calling _chunk_every_int with items, n, step

## Ventanas contiguas de exactamente `n` elementos; `n <= 0` o `n > len` dan `[]`.
weave windows with items as list of int, n as int into list of list of int:
    return calling _windows_int with items, n

## Nombre Pengunic de `windows`; misma firma y mismo resultado.
weave windowed with items as list of int, n as int into list of list of int:
    return calling _windows_int with items, n

## Pares adyacentes solapados `[[x0, x1], …]`; `len < 2` → `[]` (ver `pairwise_pairs`).
weave pairwise with items as list of int into list of list of int:
    return calling _windows_int with items, 2

## Pares adyacentes solapados como `Pair(first = xi, second = xi+1)`.
weave pairwise_pairs with items as list of int into list of Pair of int and int:
    var out as list of Pair of int and int is list of Pair of int and int
    var i as int is 0
    while i + 1 < (calling items.len):
        var pair as Pair of int and int with:
            set .first is items at i
            set .second is items at (i + 1)
        calling out.push with pair
        set i is i + 1
    return out

# --- Plegados -----------------------------------------------------------

## Suma de todos los elementos (`0` si está vacía).
weave sum with nums as list of int into int:
    return calling _sum_int with nums

## Producto de todos los elementos (`1` si está vacía).
weave product_num with nums as list of int into int:
    return calling _product_int with nums

## Mayor elemento (`0` si está vacía).
weave max_int with items as list of int into int:
    var best as int is 0
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return best
    set best is items at 0
    for x in items:
        if x > best:
            set best is x
    return best

## Menor elemento (`0` si está vacía).
weave min_int with items as list of int into int:
    var best as int is 0
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return best
    set best is items at 0
    for x in items:
        if x < best:
            set best is x
    return best

## Mínimo y máximo como `Pair(first = min, second = max)`; `[]` → `none`.
weave min_max with items as list of int into maybe Pair of int and int:
    return calling _min_max_int with items

## Núcleo de `min_max`.
weave _min_max_int with items as list of int into maybe Pair of int and int:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var lo as int is items at 0
    var hi as int is items at 0
    for x in items:
        if x < lo:
            set lo is x
        if x > hi:
            set hi is x
    var out as Pair of int and int with:
        set .first is lo
        set .second is hi
    return some out

## Media aritmética como `float` (`0.0` si está vacía).
weave mean with nums as list of int into float:
    return calling _mean_int with nums

## Suma de los cuadrados de `nums` (`0` si está vacía).
weave sum_squares with nums as list of int into int:
    var total as int is 0
    for x in nums:
        set total is total + (x * x)
    return total

## Sumas prefijas (misma longitud que `nums`); núcleo privado `_running_sum_int`.
weave running_sum with nums as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _running_sum_int with nums

## Máximos prefijas (misma longitud que `nums`).
weave running_max with nums as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _running_extreme_int with nums, true

## Mínimos prefijas (misma longitud que `nums`).
weave running_min with nums as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _running_extreme_int with nums, false

## Diferencias adyacentes `[x1 - x0, x2 - x1, …]` (`len <= 1` → `[]`).
weave differences with nums as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    if (calling nums.len) <= 1:
        return out
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling nums.len) - 1:
        calling out.push with ((nums at (i + 1)) - (nums at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Escaneo acumulativo con `f`, sembrado con el primer elemento.
##
## Misma longitud que `items` y `out[0] = items[0]`; `[]` devuelve `[]`.
weave scan_left shard T where T: Num with items as list of T, f as weave with acc as T, x as T into T into list of T:
    var n as int is calling items.len
    if n == 0:
        return for x in items when false then x
    var out as list of T is for x in items then (items at 0)
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        set out at i is (calling f with (if i > 0 then (out at (i - 1)) else donum T), (items at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return out

# --- Predicados ---------------------------------------------------------

## True si algún elemento es cero.
weave any_zero with nums as list of int into bool:
    for x in nums:
        if x == 0:
            return true
    return false

## True si todos los elementos son iguales (`len <= 1` → `true`).
weave all_equal with nums as list of int into bool:
    return (calling _is_ordered_int with nums, false, true) and (calling _is_ordered_int with nums, false, false)

## True si cada elemento es estrictamente menor que el siguiente.
weave is_strictly_asc with nums as list of int into bool:
    return calling _is_ordered_int with nums, true, true

## True si cada elemento es estrictamente mayor que el siguiente.
weave is_strictly_desc with nums as list of int into bool:
    return calling _is_ordered_int with nums, true, false

## True si `nums` está ordenada de forma no decreciente.
weave is_sorted_asc with nums as list of int into bool:
    return calling _is_ordered_int with nums, false, true

## True si `nums` está ordenada de forma no creciente.
weave is_sorted_desc with nums as list of int into bool:
    return calling _is_ordered_int with nums, false, false

## True si los elementos que cumplen `predicate` preceden a los que no.
##
## `[]` y las listas de un elemento devuelven `true`.
weave is_partitioned with items as list of int, predicate as weave with x as int into bool into bool:
    var seen_failing as bool is false
    for x in items:
        if calling predicate with x:
            if seen_failing:
                return false
        else:
            set seen_failing is true
    return true

# --- Transformaciones y combinaciones -----------------------------------

## Combina `a` y `b` con el operador `op`: `0` suma, `1` resta, `2` producto,
## `3` mínimo, `4` máximo y cualquier otro valor suma; corta en la lista corta.
weave zip_with with a as list of int, b as list of int, op as int is 0 into list of int:
    return calling _zip_with_int with a, b, op

## Núcleo de `zip_with` (ver su docstring para los códigos de `op`).
weave _zip_with_int with a as list of int, b as list of int, op as int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var limit as int is calling _pick_len_int with a, b, false
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        calling out.push with (calling _apply_op_int with (a at i), (b at i), op)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Combina `a` y `b` con la función `f`, hasta la lista más corta.
weave zip_with_op with a as list of int, b as list of int, f as weave with x as int, y as int into int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var limit as int is calling _pick_len_int with a, b, false
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        calling out.push with (calling f with (a at i), (b at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Pares `[a_i, b_i]` hasta la lista más larga, rellenando con `fill`.
weave zip_longest with a as list of int, b as list of int, fill as int is 0 into list of list of int:
    var out as list of list of int is list of list of int
    var max_len as int is calling _pick_len_int with a, b, true
    var i as int is 0
    while i < max_len:
        var pair as list of int is list of int
        calling pair.push with (if i < (calling a.len) then (a at i) else fill)
        calling pair.push with (if i < (calling b.len) then (b at i) else fill)
        calling out.push with pair
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Pares `[índice, valor]` en orden (ver `enumerate_pairs` para la variante `Pair`).
weave enumerate with items as list of int into list of list of int:
    var indexed as list of Pair of int and int is calling _enumerate_pairs_int with items
    var out as list of list of int is list of list of int
    for entry in indexed:
        var pair as list of int is list of int
        calling pair.push with entry.first
        calling pair.push with entry.second
        calling out.push with pair
    return out

## Pares `Pair(first = índice, second = valor)` en orden.
weave enumerate_pairs with items as list of int into list of Pair of int and int:
    return calling _enumerate_pairs_int with items

## Núcleo de `enumerate_pairs`.
weave _enumerate_pairs_int with items as list of int into list of Pair of int and int:
    var out as list of Pair of int and int is list of Pair of int and int
    var i as int is 0
    for x in items:
        var pair as Pair of int and int with:
            set .first is i
            set .second is x
        calling out.push with pair
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Alterna elementos de `a` y `b` hasta la lista más corta: `[a0, b0, a1, …]`.
weave interleave with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var limit as int is calling _pick_len_int with a, b, false
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        calling out.push with (a at i)
        calling out.push with (b at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Reparte por turnos todas las listas de `lists` hasta agotarlas.
weave round_robin with lists as list of list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var max_len as int is 0
    for inner in lists:
        if (calling inner.len) > max_len:
            set max_len is calling inner.len
    for step in (calling range with 0, max_len, 1):
        for inner in lists:
            if step < (calling inner.len):
                calling out.push with (inner at step)
    return out

## Rota `items` a la izquierda `k` posiciones (acepta `k` negativo).
weave rotate_left with items as list of int, k as int into list of int:
    return calling _rotate_left_int with items, k

## Rota `items` a la derecha `k` posiciones (acepta `k` negativo).
weave rotate_right with items as list of int, k as int into list of int:
    var n as int is calling items.len
    if n == 0:
        return calling _rotate_left_int with items, 0
    return calling _rotate_left_int with items, ((n - (k % n)) % n)

## Inserta `sep` entre cada par de elementos adyacentes.
weave intersperse with items as list of int, sep as int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return out
    calling out.push with (items at 0)
    var i as int is 1
    while i < (calling items.len):
        calling out.push with sep
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Aplana un nivel de anidamiento: concatena las listas de `nested`.
##
## Delega en el núcleo genérico `flatten_generic`.
weave flat_map_identity with nested as list of list of int into list of int:
    return calling flatten_generic of int with nested

## @deprecated Use `flat_map_identity` instead (misma firma y resultado).
weave flatten with nested as list of list of int into list of int:
    return calling flatten_generic of int with nested

## Aplana un nivel de anidamiento para cualquier tipo `T`.
##
## Es el núcleo genérico de `flat_map_identity` y `flatten`.
weave flatten_generic shard T with nested as list of list of T into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    for inner in nested:
        for x in inner:
            calling out.push with x
    return out

# --- Conjuntos sobre listas ordenadas -----------------------------------

## Unión deduplicada de dos listas ascendentes.
weave union_sorted with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _union_sorted_int with a, b

## Intersección deduplicada de dos listas ascendentes.
weave intersect_sorted with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _intersect_sorted_int with a, b

## Diferencia deduplicada `a \ b` de dos listas ascendentes.
weave difference_sorted with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    return calling _difference_sorted_int with a, b

## Diferencia simétrica deduplicada de dos listas ascendentes.
weave symmetric_difference_sorted with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var left as list of int is calling _difference_sorted_int with a, b
    var right as list of int is calling _difference_sorted_int with b, a
    return calling _union_sorted_int with left, right

# --- Búsqueda e índices -------------------------------------------------

## Índice de la primera aparición de `target` (`maybe none` si no está).
weave find_first with items as list of int, target as int into maybe int:
    var found as int is calling generic_index_of of int with items, target
    if found < 0:
        return maybe none
    return some found

## Índice de la última aparición de `target` (`maybe none` si no está).
weave find_last with items as list of int, target as int into maybe int:
    var i as int is (calling items.len) - 1
    while i >= 0:
        if (items at i) == target:
            return some i
        set i is i - 1
    return maybe none

## Búsqueda binaria en `sorted_items` ascendente (desordenada: indefinido).
weave binary_search with sorted_items as list of int, target as int into maybe int:
    var low as int is 0
    var high as int is (calling sorted_items.len) - 1
    while low <= high:
        var mid as int is low + ((high - low) / 2)
        var value as int is sorted_items at mid
        if value == target:
            return some mid
        if value < target:
            set low is mid + 1
        else:
            set high is mid - 1
    return maybe none

## Cuenta los elementos pares (incluye los negativos pares).
weave count_if_even with items as list of int into int:
    var count as int is 0
    for x in items:
        if (x % 2) == 0:
            set count is count + 1
    return count

## Cuenta los elementos estrictamente positivos.
weave count_if_positive with items as list of int into int:
    var count as int is 0
    for x in items:
        if x > 0:
            set count is count + 1
    return count

## Índice del primer mínimo (`maybe none` si está vacía).
weave index_min with items as list of int into maybe int:
    return calling _index_of_extreme_int with items, false

## Índice del primer máximo (`maybe none` si está vacía).
weave index_max with items as list of int into maybe int:
    return calling _index_of_extreme_int with items, true

# --- Edición estructural (pura) -----------------------------------------

## Copia con `value` insertado en `index` (índice recortado a `[0, len]`).
weave insert_at with items as list of int, index as int, value as int into list of int:
    var pos as int is index
    if pos < 0:
        set pos is 0
    if pos > (calling items.len):
        set pos is calling items.len
    var head as list of int is calling _slice_shard of int with items, 0, pos
    var tail as list of int is calling _slice_shard of int with items, pos, calling items.len
    calling head.push with value
    return calling generic_chain of int with head, tail

## Copia sin el elemento en `index` (índice fuera de rango → copia intacta).
weave remove_at with items as list of int, index as int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling items.len):
        if i != index:
            calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Copia con `value` en `index` (índice fuera de rango → copia intacta).
weave replace_at with items as list of int, index as int, value as int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling items.len):
        calling out.push with (if i == index then value else (items at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Copia con los elementos `i` y `j` intercambiados si ambos están en rango.
weave swap_at with items as list of int, i as int, j as int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is for x in items then x
    if i >= 0 and i < (calling out.len) and j >= 0 and j < (calling out.len):
        var original as int is out at i
        set out at i is (out at j)
        set out at j is original
    return out

## Copia rellenada por la izquierda con `fill` hasta `target_len`.
weave pad_left with items as list of int, target_len as int, fill as int is 0 into list of int:
    var needed as int is target_len - (calling items.len)
    return calling generic_chain of int with (calling _repeat_shard of int with fill, needed), items

## Copia rellenada por la derecha con `fill` hasta `target_len`.
weave pad_right with items as list of int, target_len as int, fill as int is 0 into list of int:
    var needed as int is target_len - (calling items.len)
    return calling generic_chain of int with items, (calling _repeat_shard of int with fill, needed)

# --- Estadística --------------------------------------------------------

## Mediana como `float`; con longitud par promedia los dos valores centrales.
weave median with items as list of int into maybe float:
    return calling _median_int with items

## Núcleo de `median`.
weave _median_int with items as list of int into maybe float:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var ordered as list of int is calling _sorted_asc_int with items
    var n as int is calling ordered.len
    var mid as int is n / 2
    if (n % 2) == 1:
        return some ((ordered at mid) to float)
    return some ((((ordered at (mid - 1)) to float) + ((ordered at mid) to float)) / 2.0)

## Valor más frecuente; en caso de empate gana el primero que alcanza el máximo.
weave mode with items as list of int into maybe int:
    return calling _mode_int with items

## Núcleo de `mode`.
weave _mode_int with items as list of int into maybe int:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var best_val as int is items at 0
    var best_count as int is 0
    for candidate in items:
        var count as int is 0
        for x in items:
            if x == candidate:
                set count is count + 1
        if count > best_count:
            set best_count is count
            set best_val is candidate
    return some best_val

## Varianza poblacional (`maybe none` si está vacía); divide entre `len`.
weave variance with items as list of int into maybe float:
    return calling _variance_int with items

## Desviación estándar poblacional (`maybe none` si está vacía).
weave stddev with items as list of int into maybe float:
    var spread as maybe float is calling _variance_int with items
    if value as float is spread:
        return some (calling arithmancy.sqrt with value)
    return maybe none

## Percentil `p` en `[0.0, 100.0]`; fuera de rango o vacía → `maybe none`.
weave percentile with items as list of int, p as float into maybe float:
    if (calling items.len) == 0 or p < 0.0 or p > 100.0:
        return maybe none
    var ordered as list of int is calling _sorted_asc_int with items
    var n as int is calling ordered.len
    var rank as float is (p / 100.0) * ((n - 1) to float)
    var low as int is rank to int
    var low_value as float is (ordered at low) to float
    if low >= n - 1:
        return some low_value
    var frac as float is rank - (low to float)
    var high_value as float is (ordered at (low + 1)) to float
    return some (low_value + (frac * (high_value - low_value)))

# --- Núcleo genérico (compatibilidad) -----------------------------------

## Primer elemento de `items`, o `default_val` si está vacía.
weave first_or shard T with items as list of T, default_val as T into T:
    if (calling items.len) > 0:
        return items at 0
    return default_val

## Primeros `n` elementos de una lista de cualquier tipo `T`.
##
## `n > len` recorta y `n < 0` da `[]`. Un cuerpo genérico no puede invocar a
## otro genérico: este `weave` es autocontenido.
weave generic_take shard T with items as list of T, n as int into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var limit as int is n
    if limit > (calling items.len):
        set limit is calling items.len
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Últimos `n` elementos de una lista de cualquier tipo `T`.
##
## `n > len` recorta y `n <= 0` da `[]`.
weave generic_take_last shard T with items as list of T, n as int into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var count as int is n
    if count > (calling items.len):
        set count is calling items.len
    if count <= 0:
        return out
    var i as int is (calling items.len) - count
    while i < (calling items.len):
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Copia invertida de una lista de cualquier tipo `T`.
weave generic_reverse shard T with items as list of T into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var i as int is (calling items.len) - 1
    while i >= 0:
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i - 1
    return out

## Concatenación de dos listas de cualquier tipo `T`.
weave generic_chain shard T with a as list of T, b as list of T into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    for x in a:
        calling out.push with x
    for x in b:
        calling out.push with x
    return out

## Índice de la primera aparición de `target` en una lista de tipo `T`, o `-1`.
##
## `T: Par` porque compara con `==`.
weave generic_index_of shard T where T: Par with items as list of T, target as T into int:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling items.len):
        if (items at i) == target:
            return i
        set i is i + 1
    return -1

# --- Helpers privados ---------------------------------------------------

## Núcleo genérico: elementos `[start_idx, end_idx)` recortado a la longitud.
weave _slice_shard shard T with items as list of T, start_idx as int, end_idx as int into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var i as int is start_idx
    while i < end_idx and i < (calling items.len):
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Núcleo genérico: descarta los `n` primeros (`n < 0` → copia completa).
weave _drop_shard shard T with items as list of T, n as int into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var start as int is n
    if start < 0:
        set start is 0
    var i as int is start
    while i < (calling items.len):
        calling out.push with (items at i)
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Núcleo genérico: `value` repetido `times` veces (`times <= 0` → `[]`).
weave _repeat_shard shard T with value as T, times as int into list of T:
    var out as list of T is list of T
    var i as int is 0
    while i < times:
        calling out.push with value
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Longitud de la más corta o de la más larga de dos listas.
weave _pick_len_int with a as list of int, b as list of int, want_max as bool into int:
    if want_max:
        return if (calling b.len) > (calling a.len) then (calling b.len) else (calling a.len)
    return if (calling b.len) < (calling a.len) then (calling b.len) else (calling a.len)

## Aplica el código de operador de `zip_with` a un par de valores.
weave _apply_op_int with va as int, vb as int, op as int into int:
    if op == 1:
        return va - vb
    if op == 2:
        return va * vb
    if op == 3:
        return if vb < va then vb else va
    if op == 4:
        return if vb > va then vb else va
    return va + vb

## Suma de enteros.
weave _sum_int with items as list of int into int:
    var total as int is 0
    for x in items:
        set total is total + x
    return total

## Producto de enteros (`1` si está vacía).
weave _product_int with items as list of int into int:
    var total as int is 1
    for x in items:
        set total is total * x
    return total

## Media aritmética (`0.0` si está vacía).
weave _mean_int with items as list of int into float:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return 0.0
    return ((calling _sum_int with items) to float) / ((calling items.len) to float)

## Varianza poblacional (`maybe none` si está vacía).
weave _variance_int with items as list of int into maybe float:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var center as float is calling _mean_int with items
    var total as float is 0.0
    for x in items:
        var diff as float is (x to float) - center
        set total is total + (diff * diff)
    return some (total / ((calling items.len) to float))

## Copia ordenada de forma ascendente (inserción, estable).
weave _sorted_asc_int with items as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is for x in items then x
    var i as int is 1
    while i < (calling out.len):
        var key as int is out at i
        var j as int is i - 1
        while j >= 0 and (out at j) > key:
            set out at (j + 1) is (out at j)
            set j is j - 1
        set out at (j + 1) is key
        set i is i + 1
    return out

## Bloques de hasta `n` elementos tomados cada `step`.
weave _chunk_every_int with items as list of int, n as int, step as int into list of list of int:
    var out as list of list of int is list of list of int
    if n <= 0 or step <= 0:
        return out
    var start_idx as int is 0
    while start_idx < (calling items.len):
        var end_idx as int is start_idx + n
        if end_idx > (calling items.len):
            set end_idx is calling items.len
        calling out.push with (calling _slice_shard of int with items, start_idx, end_idx)
        set start_idx is start_idx + step
    return out

## Ventanas contiguas de exactamente `n` elementos.
weave _windows_int with items as list of int, n as int into list of list of int:
    var out as list of list of int is list of list of int
    for block in (calling _chunk_every_int with items, n, 1):
        if (calling block.len) == n:
            calling out.push with block
    return out

## Rota a la izquierda `k` posiciones (`n == 0` → `[]`).
weave _rotate_left_int with items as list of int, k as int into list of int:
    var n as int is calling items.len
    if n == 0:
        var empty as list of int is list of int
        return empty
    var shift as int is k % n
    if shift < 0:
        set shift is shift + n
    var head as list of int is calling _slice_shard of int with items, shift, n
    var tail as list of int is calling _slice_shard of int with items, 0, shift
    return calling generic_chain of int with head, tail

## Elimina los duplicados adyacentes de una lista ordenada.
weave _dedup_int with items as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    for x in items:
        var repeated as bool is false
        if (calling out.len) > 0:
            if (out at ((calling out.len) - 1)) == x:
                set repeated is true
        if not repeated:
            calling out.push with x
    return out

## Unión deduplicada de dos listas ascendentes (resultado ascendente).
weave _union_sorted_int with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var joined as list of int is calling generic_chain of int with a, b
    return calling _dedup_int with (calling _sorted_asc_int with joined)

## Intersección deduplicada de dos listas ascendentes.
weave _intersect_sorted_int with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    for x in (calling _dedup_int with a):
        if (calling generic_index_of of int with b, x) >= 0:
            calling out.push with x
    return out

## Diferencia deduplicada `a \ b` de dos listas ascendentes.
weave _difference_sorted_int with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    for x in (calling _dedup_int with a):
        if (calling generic_index_of of int with b, x) < 0:
            calling out.push with x
    return out

## Índice del primer extremo de la lista (`maybe none` si está vacía).
weave _index_of_extreme_int with items as list of int, want_max as bool into maybe int:
    if (calling items.len) == 0:
        return maybe none
    var best_idx as int is 0
    var best_val as int is items at 0
    var i as int is 1
    while i < (calling items.len):
        var current as int is items at i
        if (want_max and current > best_val) or ((not want_max) and current < best_val):
            set best_val is current
            set best_idx is i
        set i is i + 1
    return some best_idx

## True si `items` está ordenada; `strict` exige desigualdad y `ascending` fija
## el sentido. Las listas de menos de dos elementos están ordenadas.
weave _is_ordered_int with items as list of int, strict as bool, ascending as bool into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling items.len) - 1:
        var left as int is items at i
        var right as int is items at (i + 1)
        if strict and ascending and left >= right:
            return false
        if strict and (not ascending) and left <= right:
            return false
        if (not strict) and ascending and left > right:
            return false
        if (not strict) and (not ascending) and left < right:
            return false
        set i is i + 1
    return true

## Núcleo de `running_sum`: sumas prefijas.
weave _running_sum_int with nums as list of int into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var acc as int is 0
    for x in nums:
        set acc is acc + x
        calling out.push with acc
    return out

## Extremos prefijas: máximos si `want_max`, mínimos si no.
weave _running_extreme_int with items as list of int, want_max as bool into list of int:
    var out as list of int is list of int
    var best as int is 0
    var started as bool is false
    for x in items:
        if (not started) or (want_max and x > best) or ((not want_max) and x < best):
            set best is x
            set started is true
        calling out.push with best
    return out

## Harness interno: panickea con `label` si `cond` es falso.
weave _expect with cond as bool, label as string into void:
    if not cond:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}"
## Harness interno: igualdad de escalares (int, float, bool).
weave _expect_eq shard T where T: Par with actual as T, expected as T, label as string into void:
    if actual != expected:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}"
## Harness interno: igualdad de flotantes con tolerancia.
weave _expect_float_near with actual as float, expected as float, tolerance as float, label as string into void:
    var diff as float is actual - expected
    if diff < 0.0:
        set diff is 0.0 - diff
    if diff > tolerance:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: float"
## Harness interno: igualdad de listas de enteros (longitud y elementos).
weave _expect_eq_ints with actual as list of int, expected as list of int, label as string into void:
    if (calling actual.len) != (calling expected.len):
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: len {(calling actual.len)} != {(calling expected.len)}"
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling actual.len):
        if (actual at i) != (expected at i):
            calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: [{i}]"
        set i is i + 1
## Harness interno: igualdad de listas de listas de enteros.
weave _expect_eq_chunks with actual as list of list of int, expected as list of list of int, label as string into void:
    if (calling actual.len) != (calling expected.len):
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: outer len"
    var i as int is 0
    while i < (calling actual.len):
        calling _expect_eq_ints with (actual at i), (expected at i), label
        set i is i + 1
## Harness interno: `maybe T` presente e igual a `expected`.
weave _expect_some shard T where T: Par with m as maybe T, expected as T, label as string into void:
    if value as T is m:
        if value != expected:
            calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}"
    else:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: none"
## Harness interno: par de enteros (el `Pair` va al final por el parser).
weave _expect_pair with first_expected as int, second_expected as int, label as string, pair as Pair of int and int into void:
    if pair.first != first_expected:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: first {pair.first} != {first_expected}"
    if pair.second != second_expected:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: second {pair.second} != {second_expected}"
## Harness interno: `maybe Pair` presente e igual a los dos valores.
weave _expect_some_pair with first_expected as int, second_expected as int, label as string, m as maybe Pair of int and int into void:
    if pair as Pair of int and int is m:
        calling _expect_pair with first_expected, second_expected, label, pair
    else:
        calling spark.panic with "loom test failed: {label}: none"

# --- Tests ---
# Harness privado `_expect*` (ver `## Notas de diseño`).

# Generación de secuencias
test "range genera el intervalo semiabierto":
    var exp as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling range with 1, 5, 1), exp, "range"
test "range con paso mayor que uno":
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling range with 0, 10, 3), (calling unfold_range with 0, 4, 3), "range paso"
test "range con paso negativo recorre hacia atrás":
    var exp as list of int is [5, 3, 1]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling range with 5, 0, -2), exp, "range desc"
test "range con paso cero devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling range with 0, 5, 0), empty, "range step 0"
test "range con start mayor que end y paso positivo queda vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling range with 5, 1, 1), empty, "range invertido"
test "unfold_range produce count elementos":
    var exp as list of int is [5, 7, 9]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling unfold_range with 5, 3, 2), exp, "unfold"
test "unfold_range con paso negativo desciende":
    var exp as list of int is [5, 3, 1]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling unfold_range with 5, 3, -2), exp, "unfold desc"
test "unfold_range con count no positivo devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling unfold_range with 1, 0, 1), empty, "unfold count 0"
test "repeat repite el valor times veces":
    var exp as list of int is [7, 7, 7]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling repeat with 7, 3), exp, "repeat"
test "repeat con times cero o negativo devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling repeat with 7, 0), empty, "repeat 0"
test "repeat con times negativo devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling repeat with 7, -2), empty, "repeat negativo"

# Cortes y composición
test "take devuelve los primeros n":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var exp as list of int is [1, 2]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling take with xs, 2), exp, "take"
test "take recorta cuando n supera la longitud":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling take with xs, 9), xs, "take largo"
test "take con n cero devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling take with xs, 0), empty, "take 0"
test "take con n negativo devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling take with xs, -1), empty, "take negativo"
test "skip descarta los primeros n":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var exp as list of int is [3, 4]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling skip with xs, 2), exp, "skip"
test "skip con n mayor que la longitud devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling skip with xs, 5), empty, "skip largo"
test "skip con n cero devuelve una copia":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling skip with xs, 0), xs, "skip 0"
test "take de la lista vacía devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling take with empty, 3), empty, "take vacía"
test "skip de la lista vacía devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling skip with empty, 3), empty, "skip vacía"
test "skip con n negativo equivale a cero":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling skip with xs, -3), xs, "skip negativo"
test "chain concatena dos listas":
    var a as list of int is [1, 2]
    var b as list of int is [3, 4]
    var exp as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling chain with a, b), exp, "chain"
test "chain con la segunda lista vacía devuelve la primera":
    var a as list of int is [1]
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    calling _expect_eq_ints with (calling chain with a, empty), a, "chain vacía"

# Bloques y ventanas
test "chunks divide en bloques exactos":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunks with xs, 2
    var first as list of int is blocks at 0
    var second as list of int is blocks at 1
    calling _expect_eq_ints with first, (calling unfold_range with 1, 2, 1), "chunks 0"
    calling _expect_eq_ints with second, (calling unfold_range with 3, 2, 1), "chunks 1"
test "chunks deja el último bloque corto":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunks with xs, 2
    var last as list of int is blocks at 2
    calling _expect_eq_ints with last, (calling unfold_range with 5, 1, 1), "chunks corto"
test "chunks con n no positivo devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var empty as list of list of int is list of list of int
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling chunks with xs, 0), empty, "chunks 0"
test "chunks con n mayor que la longitud devuelve un bloque":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunks with xs, 5
    calling _expect_eq with (calling blocks.len), 1, "chunks grande"
test "windows con n cero devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var none as list of list of int is list of list of int
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling windows with xs, 0), none, "windows 0"
test "chunk_every solapa cuando step es menor que n":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunk_every with xs, 3, 1
    var last as list of int is blocks at 3
    calling _expect_eq with (calling blocks.len), 4, "chunk_every solape"
    calling _expect_eq_ints with last, (calling unfold_range with 4, 1, 1), "chunk_every último"
test "chunk_every con step igual a n equivale a chunks":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunk_every with xs, 2, 2
    var first as list of int is blocks at 0
    var second as list of int is blocks at 1
    calling _expect_eq_ints with first, (calling unfold_range with 1, 2, 1), "chunk_every 0"
    calling _expect_eq_ints with second, (calling unfold_range with 3, 2, 1), "chunk_every 1"
test "chunk_every con step mayor que n salta elementos":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    var blocks as list of list of int is calling chunk_every with xs, 2, 3
    var second as list of int is blocks at 1
    var exp as list of int is [4, 5]
    calling _expect_eq_ints with second, exp, "chunk_every salto"
test "chunk_every con n o step no positivos devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var empty as list of list of int is list of list of int
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling chunk_every with xs, 0, 1), empty, "chunk_every n 0"
test "windows produce todas las ventanas completas":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3, 4]
    var wins as list of list of int is calling windows with xs, 3
    var first as list of int is wins at 0
    var last as list of int is wins at 1
    calling _expect_eq_ints with first, (calling unfold_range with 1, 3, 1), "windows 0"
    calling _expect_eq_ints with last, (calling unfold_range with 2, 3, 1), "windows 1"
test "windows con n igual a la longitud devuelve una ventana":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var wins as list of list of int is calling windows with xs, 2
    calling _expect_eq with (calling wins.len), 1, "windows exacta"
test "windows con n mayor que la longitud devuelve vacío":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2]
    var empty as list of list of int is list of list of int
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling windows with xs, 5), empty, "windows grande"
test "windows con n cero o lista vacía devuelve vacío":
    var empty as list of int is list of int
    var none_windows as list of list of int is list of list of int
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling windows with empty, 2), none_windows, "windows vacía"
test "windowed es el nombre Pengunic de windows":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
    calling _expect_eq_chunks with (calling _windows_int with xs, 2), (calling windows with xs, 2), "windowed"
test "pairwise devuelve pares solapados":
    var xs as list of int is [1, 2, 3]
    var pairs as list of list of int is calling pairwise with xs
    var first as list of int is pairs at 0
    calling _expect_eq with (calling pairs.len), 2, "pairwise len"
